@startuml

title ores.shell.storage Component

set namespaceSeparator ::

namespace ores #F2F2F2 {
    namespace shell #F2F2F2 {
        namespace app #F2F2F2 {
            namespace commands #F2F2F2 {
                class objects_operations_commands {
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' The unit is generated from the storage operation model, so its methods are
' the model's messages: one process_* per message that declares a subject and a
' response. It is a NATS client like every other shell command unit — the same
' verbs serve the HTTP path too, because both interfaces answer the same
' operation set.

class ores::shell::app::commands::objects_operations_commands #ECECEC {
    {static} +register_commands(root_menu : Menu, session : nats_client) : void
    {static} +process_put_objects(out : ostream, session : nats_client, args : vector<string>) : void
    {static} +process_get_objects(out : ostream, session : nats_client, args : vector<string>) : void
    {static} +process_delete_objects(out : ostream, session : nats_client, args : vector<string>) : void
    {static} +process_list_objects(out : ostream, session : nats_client, args : vector<string>) : void
}
note right of "ores::shell::app::commands::objects_operations_commands"
The raw surface: every verb takes a bucket, a key and a
local path, so a caller that only wants bytes somewhere
does not have to learn a domain verb. The consumer verbs
that wrap storage live with their own domains.
end note

